A||||1||fierohoho||Speaker polarity (+)(-) ?||||1||
Z||000000||fierohoho||12-17-2001||02:19 PM||||Does anyone know how to tell or test to see which terminal on an unmarked speaker is positive (+) and which is negative (-)?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-17-2001||02:27 PM||||Usually the terminal size is different. The positive is bigger. If terminals are same size and there is no dot or "+" marking, you can check it with a AA battery. When the positive side of the battery is hooked to the positive side of the speaker (and negative to negative) the cone will move out. If the positive of the battery is hooked to the negative the speaker (and negative of battery to positive of speaker) will draw itself in. Don't leave it hooked up constantly. Just a quick check is all you need.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">            <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
